{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":309162,"duration_api_ms":309110,"num_turns":1,"result":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Man pages omit edge cases and exit-code contracts. This project derives formal specs from C source code, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies them through differential testing.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline: extract (C source) → specify (human-authored PRDs via make-work/do-work skills) → synthesize (mage-claude-orchestrator drives Claude agent) → verify (differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries). Key components: `cmd/` (per-utility binaries), `pkg/sys|format|testutils` (shared library), `docs/` (specs, human-authored), `magefiles/` (build boundary).\n\n**Current State**: No generated Go code on the working branch. All generated code lives at `generation-merged` tags from three prior pipeline runs. All foundational packages (testutils, sys, format) and early utilities (ts, wc, cat, sponge) are spec-complete; their code is at tags only.\n\n**Current Release**: Release 01.1 — one use case: `rel01.1-uc001-cat` (specstatus: spec_complete, codestatus: not started). This is the earliest incomplete release.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 01.1 has a single use case (cat) with specs complete and no code. Per P2, implementation and tests must be split; per P8, implementation precedes tests. The constraint limits this session to 1 task — the implementation task comes first.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement cmd/cat file concatenation and output transformation (prd-cat R1-R4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - \"docs/specs/product-requirements/prd-cat.yaml (if this path does not exist, list docs/specs/product-requirements/ and read the file matching prd[0-9]+-cat.yaml before writing any code)\"\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel01.1-uc001-cat.yaml\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-01.1.yaml\n      - \"docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (cmd/ component structure; design decision 7 for generation scope exclusions)\"\n      - go.mod\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/cat/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: complete cat implementation -- flag parsing, input loop, line transformation, exit codes\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement all flags per the cat PRD: -n (number all output lines), -b (number nonempty lines, overrides -n for those lines), -s (suppress repeated empty output lines), -E (append $ to each line end), -T (display TAB as ^I), -v (display nonprinting characters using caret and M- notation), combined aliases -A (equivalent to -vET), -e (equivalent to -vE), -t (equivalent to -vT), and -u (accepted and silently ignored for POSIX compatibility)\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Process operands per the cat PRD: when no operands are given or an operand is '-', read from stdin; for each named file operand, open and process in order; on open failure write 'cat: <name>: <error>' to stderr, record failure, and continue to the next operand\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Apply line transformation per the cat PRD in pipeline order: -v nonprinting escapes (DEL=^?, high-bit bytes use M- prefix, other control chars use caret notation), then -T tab replacement (TAB->^I), then -E end-of-line marker ($), then -n/-b line numbering (right-justified in 6-character field followed by tab, counting from 1; -b omits blank lines from numbering), then -s consecutive-blank-line suppression\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement exit code contract per the cat PRD: exit 0 when all operands are read and all output is written without error; exit nonzero when any operand cannot be opened or when a write error occurs on stdout\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Package cmd/cat with primary source file main.go (package main); module github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils per go.mod; this task produces the implementation only -- differential tests are a separate follow-on task\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"cat does not depend on pkg/sys, pkg/format, or pkg/testutils; implement all logic inline in main.go without importing those packages\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Derive all implementation decisions -- flag names, default values, error message format, nonprinting character encoding, and edge case handling -- from the cat PRD, not from this task description\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: go build ./cmd/cat/ succeeds with no compilation errors\n      - id: AC2\n        text: go vet ./cmd/cat/ produces no diagnostic output\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Invoked with no arguments, the binary reads stdin and writes to stdout unchanged (byte-for-byte passthrough)\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Invoked with -n, every output line is prefixed with a right-justified line number in a 6-character field followed by a tab character, counting from 1\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Invoked with -b, only nonempty output lines receive a number prefix; blank lines are emitted without a number\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"Invoked with a nonexistent filename, the binary writes an error message to stderr and exits nonzero without panicking\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"All flags defined in the cat PRD are accepted by the binary without 'flag provided but not defined' errors\"\n```","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"adb1e713-b58c-4f32-bf1e-9adf642185a5","total_cost_usd":0.5989545000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15840,"cache_read_input_tokens":19189,"output_tokens":19614,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15840,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"out